  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 18,
    "summary": "A fool’s mouth is his destruction—Whoever obtains a wife obtains a good thing—A man who has friends must show himself friendly.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Through desire a man, having separated himself, seeketh and intermeddleth with all wisdom.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A fool hath no delight in understanding, but that his heart may discover itself.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When the wicked cometh, then cometh also contempt, and with ignominy reproach.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The words of a man’s mouth are as deep waters, and the wellspring of wisdom as a flowing brook.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Prov. 20:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 50
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It is not good to accept the person of the wicked, to overthrow the righteous in judgment.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Ps. 82:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A fool’s lips enter into contention, and his mouth calleth for strokes.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Contention."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A fool’s mouth is his destruction, and his lips are the snare of his soul.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Prov. 10:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "Ps. 64:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The words of a talebearer are as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "OR slanderer. TG Gossip; Honesty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He also that is slothful in his work is brother to him that is a great waster.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "TG Waste."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The name of the Lord is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "2 Sam. 22:3; Ps. 61:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 23
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The rich man’s wealth is his strong city, and as an high wall in his own conceit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Matt. 19:24 (16–24)."
          },
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Prov. 10:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 24
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Before destruction the heart of man is haughty, and before honour is humility.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Prov. 29:23."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Alma 7:23 (23–24); D&C 112:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that answereth a matter before he heareth it, it is folly and shame unto him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Rashness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The spirit of a man will sustain his infirmity; but a wounded spirit who can bear?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The heart of the prudent getteth knowledge; and the ear of the wise seeketh knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Prudence."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Knowledge."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man’s gift maketh room for him, and bringeth him before great men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that is first in his own cause seemeth just; but his neighbour cometh and searcheth him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Mark 9:35."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The lot causeth contentions to cease, and parteth between the mighty.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "Prov. 16:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A brother offended is harder to be won than a strong city: and their contentions are like the bars of a castle.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood."
          },
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Offense."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Contention."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 68
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man’s belly shall be satisfied with the fruit of his mouth; and with the increase of his lips shall he be filled.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Death and life are in the power of the tongue: and they that love it shall eat the fruit thereof.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Matt. 12:37 (34–37); Alma 12:14."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso findeth a wife findeth a good thing, and obtaineth favour of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "JST Prov. 18:22 Whoso findeth a good wife hath obtained favor of the Lord."
          },
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Wives."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The poor useth entreaties; but the rich answereth roughly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Prov. 19:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "Alma 32:5 (1–5)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man that hath friends must shew himself friendly: and there is a friend that sticketh closer than a brother.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "Prov. 27:10. TG Friendship."
          },
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 109,
            "text": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
